class Solution {
    public int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
        int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int currentSum = 0;
        
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            currentSum += nums[i];
            
            if (currentSum > maxSum) {
                maxSum = currentSum;
            }
            
            if (currentSum < 0) {
                currentSum = 0;
            }
        }
        
        return maxSum;
    }
}

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n)
- **Space Complexity:** O(1)

### Explanation
- We traverse the array only once.
- At each position, we decide whether to start a new subarray or extend the current subarray.
- We only use variables to store the current sum and maximum sum.
- No extra array or data structure is required, so the space complexity is **O(1)**.
